1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,450
Transition questions look easy.

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:05,860
One blank, four short
choices like however,

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:09,060
therefore, and for example.

4
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:12,379
But they're easy to miss,
because if you plug each word in,

5
00:00:12,399 --> 00:00:15,010
two or three of them can sound fine.

6
00:00:15,476 --> 00:00:19,886
The fix is to decide what the blank
needs before you look at the choices.

7
00:00:20,197 --> 00:00:24,456
In this video: the seven
relationships transitions show,

8
00:00:24,476 --> 00:00:27,606
the words in each group, a simple method,

9
00:00:27,715 --> 00:00:32,367
and seven SAT-style questions,
including the traps.

10
00:00:32,815 --> 00:00:35,475
A transition doesn't add information.

11
00:00:35,495 --> 00:00:39,145
It tells you how two ideas connect.

12
00:00:39,295 --> 00:00:43,235
So the real question is: what's the
relationship between the sentence before the

13
00:00:43,255 --> 00:00:45,384
blank and the sentence after it?

14
00:00:45,833 --> 00:00:47,883
There are seven to know.

15
00:00:47,993 --> 00:00:49,893
One: contrast.

16
00:00:49,913 --> 00:00:52,453
The next idea goes against the last one.

17
00:00:52,473 --> 00:00:56,093
However, but, yet, in
contrast, by contrast,

18
00:00:56,113 --> 00:00:57,253
on the other hand.

19
00:00:57,273 --> 00:00:59,363
Concession is a close cousin.

20
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:03,573
Nevertheless, nonetheless, even so, still.

21
00:01:03,593 --> 00:01:05,963
It means: despite that.

22
00:01:06,407 --> 00:01:08,777
Two: cause and effect.

23
00:01:09,126 --> 00:01:10,747
The next idea is a result.

24
00:01:10,767 --> 00:01:14,187
Therefore, thus,
consequently, as a result,

25
00:01:14,207 --> 00:01:15,577
for this reason.

26
00:01:15,806 --> 00:01:17,577
Three: addition.

27
00:01:18,007 --> 00:01:19,667
More of the same kind of point.

28
00:01:19,687 --> 00:01:23,187
Moreover, furthermore,
additionally, in addition,

29
00:01:23,207 --> 00:01:24,337
also.

30
00:01:24,487 --> 00:01:27,977
Similarly and likewise
add a parallel case.

31
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,350
Four: example.

32
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:34,870
The next sentence is a specific
case of a general claim.

33
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:37,909
For example, for instance, to illustrate.

34
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:41,200
Five: sequence or time.

35
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:45,440
First, next, then, later, subsequently,

36
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:47,390
meanwhile, finally.

37
00:01:47,883 --> 00:01:50,423
Six: emphasis or clarification.

38
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:53,863
In fact and indeed push
the same idea further.

39
00:01:53,883 --> 00:01:57,303
In other words and that is
restate it more clearly.

40
00:01:57,323 --> 00:01:59,372
Seven: conclusion.

41
00:01:59,442 --> 00:02:04,173
In conclusion, in sum, in short, overall.

42
00:02:04,615 --> 00:02:06,514
You don't need to memorize every word.

43
00:02:06,534 --> 00:02:09,595
You need to know which
group each one belongs to,

44
00:02:09,615 --> 00:02:13,865
because the SAT is really
asking which group fits.

45
00:02:14,350 --> 00:02:15,600
Here's the format.

46
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:20,530
A short passage with a blank, often
at the start of the last sentence.

47
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:25,530
The question says: which choice
completes the text with the most logical

48
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:26,560
transition?

49
00:02:27,026 --> 00:02:31,486
To answer it, read the sentence before
the blank and the sentence after it.

50
00:02:31,506 --> 00:02:33,406
Sometimes you need the whole passage,

51
00:02:33,426 --> 00:02:37,036
because the last sentence can
connect back to an earlier one.

52
00:02:37,505 --> 00:02:40,045
And watch how fragile the logic is.

53
00:02:40,065 --> 00:02:41,795
The trail was steep.

54
00:02:41,825 --> 00:02:45,084
blank the hikers moved slowly.

55
00:02:45,104 --> 00:02:47,315
That's cause and effect: therefore.

56
00:02:47,777 --> 00:02:49,707
Now change one word.

57
00:02:50,297 --> 00:02:52,467
The trail was steep.

58
00:02:52,737 --> 00:02:55,167
blank the hikers moved quickly.

59
00:02:55,187 --> 00:02:57,447
Now it's a surprise, so it's a contrast:

60
00:02:57,467 --> 00:02:58,327
however.

61
00:02:58,347 --> 00:03:02,597
Same sentences, one word different,
and the transition flips.

62
00:03:03,105 --> 00:03:04,435
So here's the method.

63
00:03:04,505 --> 00:03:06,884
Step one: cover the choices.

64
00:03:06,904 --> 00:03:08,445
Don't look at them yet.

65
00:03:08,465 --> 00:03:13,434
Step two: read the sentence before
the blank and the sentence after it.

66
00:03:13,843 --> 00:03:18,012
Step three: name the
relationship in a word or two.

67
00:03:18,083 --> 00:03:19,083
Against?

68
00:03:19,163 --> 00:03:20,183
Result?

69
00:03:20,203 --> 00:03:21,463
More of the same?

70
00:03:21,483 --> 00:03:22,743
An example?

71
00:03:22,763 --> 00:03:24,222
Later in time?

72
00:03:24,242 --> 00:03:28,623
Step four: uncover the choices,
find the one from that group,

73
00:03:28,643 --> 00:03:32,013
and read the sentence with it
in place to make sure it works.

74
00:03:32,491 --> 00:03:33,491
Let's try it.

75
00:03:33,931 --> 00:03:39,031
Venus is sometimes called Earth's twin
because the two planets are similar in

76
00:03:39,051 --> 00:03:40,860
size and structure.

77
00:03:41,111 --> 00:03:45,351
blank the surface of Venus
is far hotter than Earth's:

78
00:03:45,371 --> 00:03:47,901
it is hot enough to melt lead.

79
00:03:48,431 --> 00:03:49,921
Pause and try it.

80
00:03:55,781 --> 00:03:59,270
Before the blank: Venus is like Earth.

81
00:03:59,301 --> 00:04:01,481
After it: Venus is very different.

82
00:04:01,501 --> 00:04:02,561
That's a contrast.

83
00:04:02,581 --> 00:04:04,871
Predict: however, or but.

84
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:07,151
The answer is A, however.

85
00:04:07,616 --> 00:04:11,236
Similarly would mean
Venus is like Earth again.

86
00:04:11,256 --> 00:04:15,905
Therefore would mean being
Earth's twin causes the heat.

87
00:04:16,216 --> 00:04:19,956
And the heat isn't an example
of the two planets being alike,

88
00:04:19,976 --> 00:04:22,906
so for example doesn't work either.

89
00:04:23,326 --> 00:04:24,586
Question two.

90
00:04:24,606 --> 00:04:31,026
Unlike most substances, water is less
dense in its solid form than in its liquid

91
00:04:31,046 --> 00:04:31,896
form.

92
00:04:31,916 --> 00:04:37,906
blank ice floats on the surface of lakes
and ponds instead of sinking to the

93
00:04:37,926 --> 00:04:38,926
bottom.

94
00:04:39,158 --> 00:04:40,648
Pause and try it.

95
00:04:46,508 --> 00:04:50,637
Before: solid water is less
dense than liquid water.

96
00:04:50,708 --> 00:04:52,958
After: ice floats.

97
00:04:53,068 --> 00:04:57,248
Things that are less dense float, so
the second sentence is the result of the

98
00:04:57,268 --> 00:04:58,168
first.

99
00:04:58,188 --> 00:05:01,127
Predict: therefore, or as a result.

100
00:05:01,147 --> 00:05:02,198
That's D.

101
00:05:02,629 --> 00:05:04,449
Nevertheless is the trap.

102
00:05:04,469 --> 00:05:08,129
The phrase unlike most substances
sounds like a contrast.

103
00:05:08,149 --> 00:05:11,688
But that contrast is
inside the first sentence.

104
00:05:11,708 --> 00:05:14,529
Between the two sentences,
it's cause and effect.

105
00:05:14,549 --> 00:05:18,729
Nevertheless would mean ice
floats despite being less dense,

106
00:05:18,749 --> 00:05:20,359
which is backwards.

107
00:05:20,879 --> 00:05:22,179
Question three.

108
00:05:22,199 --> 00:05:26,449
Some animals turn objects from
their surroundings into tools.

109
00:05:26,659 --> 00:05:30,798
blank New Caledonian crows
break twigs off bushes,

110
00:05:30,818 --> 00:05:36,589
trim them into sticks, and use the sticks
to pull insects out of holes in logs.

111
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,535
Pause and try it.

112
00:05:44,395 --> 00:05:46,815
The first sentence is a general claim:

113
00:05:46,835 --> 00:05:49,165
some animals make tools.

114
00:05:49,315 --> 00:05:53,044
The second is one specific case: crows.

115
00:05:53,435 --> 00:05:56,655
General, then specific, means example.

116
00:05:56,675 --> 00:05:59,005
The answer is B, for instance.

117
00:05:59,545 --> 00:06:01,435
In other words is the tempting one.

118
00:06:01,784 --> 00:06:05,045
But in other words means the next
sentence says the same thing again.

119
00:06:05,065 --> 00:06:06,685
This one doesn't restate the claim.

120
00:06:06,705 --> 00:06:09,755
It adds a new, narrower case.

121
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:11,533
Question four.

122
00:06:11,763 --> 00:06:16,663
The Svalbard Global Seed Vault, built
inside a mountain on a remote Arctic

123
00:06:16,683 --> 00:06:21,943
island, stores backup copies of seeds
from gene banks around the world.

124
00:06:21,963 --> 00:06:27,103
The vault sits well above sea level, so
it should stay dry even if sea levels

125
00:06:27,123 --> 00:06:28,123
rise.

126
00:06:28,243 --> 00:06:33,263
blank the permafrost and thick rock
surrounding the vault would keep the seeds

127
00:06:33,283 --> 00:06:35,773
frozen even if the power failed.

128
00:06:36,258 --> 00:06:37,748
Pause and try it.

129
00:06:43,608 --> 00:06:47,617
Before the blank: one way
the vault protects the seeds.

130
00:06:47,648 --> 00:06:49,818
After it: a second way.

131
00:06:49,928 --> 00:06:52,788
Two separate points,
pointing the same direction.

132
00:06:52,808 --> 00:06:53,948
That's addition.

133
00:06:53,968 --> 00:06:56,778
The answer is B, additionally.

134
00:06:57,242 --> 00:06:59,222
For this reason is the trap.

135
00:06:59,242 --> 00:07:01,982
Being above sea level
doesn't cause the permafrost.

136
00:07:02,002 --> 00:07:05,461
Two facts side by side
aren't cause and effect.

137
00:07:05,481 --> 00:07:07,662
And nonetheless would need a contrast,

138
00:07:07,682 --> 00:07:08,861
which isn't there.

139
00:07:08,881 --> 00:07:12,701
Instead would mean one
protection replaces the other,

140
00:07:12,721 --> 00:07:14,652
but the vault has both.

141
00:07:15,192 --> 00:07:16,772
Question five.

142
00:07:16,792 --> 00:07:22,252
In nineteen twenty-eight, Alexander
Fleming noticed that a mold growing in one

143
00:07:22,272 --> 00:07:26,362
of his laboratory dishes had
killed the bacteria around it.

144
00:07:26,492 --> 00:07:32,032
blank in nineteen forty, a team at
the University of Oxford showed that a

145
00:07:32,052 --> 00:07:35,471
purified form of the
substance the mold produced,

146
00:07:35,491 --> 00:07:40,422
penicillin, could protect mice
from a deadly bacterial infection.

147
00:07:40,925 --> 00:07:42,415
Pause and try it.

148
00:07:48,275 --> 00:07:49,925
The dates are your clue.

149
00:07:49,995 --> 00:07:53,005
Nineteen twenty-eight,
then nineteen forty.

150
00:07:53,195 --> 00:07:56,814
One event happened, and
then, twelve years on,

151
00:07:56,834 --> 00:07:58,055
another one did.

152
00:07:58,075 --> 00:07:59,325
That's sequence.

153
00:07:59,475 --> 00:08:02,245
The answer is A, later.

154
00:08:02,693 --> 00:08:06,993
Instead would mean the Oxford
work replaced Fleming's discovery.

155
00:08:07,013 --> 00:08:07,953
It built on it.

156
00:08:07,973 --> 00:08:11,113
The experiment isn't an
example of his observation,

157
00:08:11,133 --> 00:08:13,033
and it isn't a restatement either.

158
00:08:13,053 --> 00:08:14,422
It's a new event.

159
00:08:14,927 --> 00:08:16,297
Now the traps.

160
00:08:16,407 --> 00:08:20,067
Trap one: two choices
that do the same job.

161
00:08:20,087 --> 00:08:23,587
If therefore and as a
result are both choices,

162
00:08:23,607 --> 00:08:24,986
they mean the same thing.

163
00:08:25,006 --> 00:08:27,427
They can't both be the one right answer,

164
00:08:27,447 --> 00:08:29,816
so usually neither is.

165
00:08:30,249 --> 00:08:34,229
Trap two: the however
versus therefore flip.

166
00:08:34,249 --> 00:08:35,429
They're opposites.

167
00:08:35,449 --> 00:08:38,388
Therefore says the next
idea is what you'd expect.

168
00:08:38,408 --> 00:08:41,189
However says it goes
against what you'd expect.

169
00:08:41,209 --> 00:08:45,578
If you're stuck between them, ask:
is the second sentence a surprise?

170
00:08:46,099 --> 00:08:50,559
Trap three: grabbing a contrast word
because you noticed a contrast somewhere in

171
00:08:50,579 --> 00:08:51,479
the passage.

172
00:08:51,499 --> 00:08:54,869
Only the relationship
across the blank counts.

173
00:08:55,370 --> 00:08:56,750
Question six.

174
00:08:56,770 --> 00:09:01,870
In nineteen thirty-five, cane toads were
brought to Australia to control beetles

175
00:09:01,890 --> 00:09:04,340
that were damaging sugarcane crops.

176
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:08,820
blank the toads had no
noticeable effect on the beetles.

177
00:09:09,301 --> 00:09:10,791
Pause and try it.

178
00:09:17,651 --> 00:09:20,390
The toads were brought in
to control the beetles.

179
00:09:20,410 --> 00:09:22,911
Then they had no noticeable effect.

180
00:09:22,931 --> 00:09:24,381
Is that what you'd expect?

181
00:09:24,451 --> 00:09:25,071
No.

182
00:09:25,091 --> 00:09:26,551
The plan failed.

183
00:09:26,571 --> 00:09:28,911
That's a surprise, so it's a contrast:

184
00:09:28,931 --> 00:09:29,790
however.

185
00:09:29,810 --> 00:09:31,661
The answer is C.

186
00:09:32,128 --> 00:09:33,818
Now look at A and B.

187
00:09:34,087 --> 00:09:36,748
Therefore and as a result do the same job,

188
00:09:36,768 --> 00:09:39,068
so they can't both be right.

189
00:09:39,088 --> 00:09:41,948
And they'd both say the
plan caused the failure,

190
00:09:41,968 --> 00:09:43,388
which makes no sense.

191
00:09:43,408 --> 00:09:45,617
For example doesn't fit either.

192
00:09:46,015 --> 00:09:47,105
Here's the flip.

193
00:09:47,415 --> 00:09:52,265
If the first sentence had said the
toads couldn't reach the beetles,

194
00:09:52,375 --> 00:09:54,304
then therefore would work.

195
00:09:54,334 --> 00:09:57,835
The words around the blank
decide the transition,

196
00:09:57,855 --> 00:09:59,185
not the topic.

197
00:09:59,715 --> 00:10:01,415
Last one, and it's harder.

198
00:10:01,435 --> 00:10:04,495
The first telegraph cable laid
across the Atlantic Ocean,

199
00:10:04,515 --> 00:10:09,845
completed in eighteen fifty-eight, stopped
working after only about three weeks.

200
00:10:10,045 --> 00:10:15,315
blank the short-lived cable proved that
an undersea cable could carry messages

201
00:10:15,335 --> 00:10:17,825
between Europe and North America.

202
00:10:18,279 --> 00:10:19,019
Pause and try it.

203
00:10:19,039 --> 00:10:20,689
Take a little longer on this one.

204
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,510
The cable failed fast.

205
00:10:31,020 --> 00:10:33,040
But it still proved the idea worked.

206
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:37,189
The relationship is: despite that.

207
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:40,430
So the answer is B, nevertheless.

208
00:10:40,923 --> 00:10:46,093
Here's why in contrast is wrong, even
though it's also a contrast word.

209
00:10:46,763 --> 00:10:49,062
In contrast compares two different things,

210
00:10:49,082 --> 00:10:51,773
like two planets or two telescopes.

211
00:10:51,803 --> 00:10:54,583
This passage has only
one thing, the cable.

212
00:10:54,603 --> 00:10:56,492
There's nothing to compare it to.

213
00:10:56,933 --> 00:11:00,353
Consequently would mean the
failure caused the proof.

214
00:11:00,373 --> 00:11:02,953
And nothing here is an example.

215
00:11:02,973 --> 00:11:07,863
So the rule from earlier
needs one adjustment.

216
00:11:08,053 --> 00:11:09,953
True synonyms are both out.

217
00:11:09,973 --> 00:11:14,423
But two words from the same family
can still do different jobs.

218
00:11:14,869 --> 00:11:16,849
Here's the method on one card.

219
00:11:16,869 --> 00:11:18,329
Cover the choices.

220
00:11:18,349 --> 00:11:21,489
Read the sentence before
and after the blank.

221
00:11:21,509 --> 00:11:22,808
Name the relationship.

222
00:11:22,828 --> 00:11:25,479
Then match the group, and read it back in.

223
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:30,140
If you're stuck between two
choices, ask the sharper question.

224
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:33,860
Is the second idea
expected, or a surprise?

225
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:38,460
Are two things being compared, or
is one idea true despite another?

226
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,490
That usually breaks the tie.

227
00:11:41,020 --> 00:11:41,920
Recap.

228
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:45,830
Transitions test
relationships, not vocabulary.

229
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:48,999
Predict the relationship
first, then find it.

230
00:11:49,019 --> 00:11:53,399
Watch for same-job pairs, the
however versus therefore flip,

231
00:11:53,419 --> 00:11:55,950
and contrast versus concession.

232
00:11:56,404 --> 00:12:00,504
For more practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter for

233
00:12:00,524 --> 00:12:03,614
transitions under Expression of Ideas.

234
00:12:04,083 --> 00:12:08,103
All the questions in this video
were written for this video,

235
00:12:08,123 --> 00:12:10,663
in the style of the real test.

236
00:12:10,683 --> 00:12:12,783
If this helped, subscribe.

237
00:12:12,803 --> 00:12:16,892
Next up: command of evidence
questions with tables and graphs.
